anations and switch routes.","Teacher, student and caregiver reviewers need accessible ways to challenge reading burden, visibility, participation and workload."],"message":"Build integrates revised Design (29) and the implementation challenge (35). Sequence 27 was a hypothetical loss of qualified wording, not an observed defect; the candidate implements deliberate replacement and recovery. Clearing now recreates entry controls and removes application-owned previews, proposals and recovery copies. No execution, interaction testing, human approval or field evidence exists. Proceed to synthetic interaction review and preparation for human review within the rehearsal.","objections":["Hypothetical learner dissent: “Trying a suggestion should not erase my uncertainty.” Recovery remains deliberate and inspectable.","Hypothetical teacher dissent: paper-only discussion may leave more time for reasoning than device management.","Rivals and unknowns: sparse writing may reflect reading, typing or pressure; fluent wording may reflect copying or recorder influence. Languages, device access and discussion norms remain unknown."],"prototype_html":"<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Fictional evidence workbench</title><style>body{font:17px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:960px;margin:auto;padding:20px;color:#172638;background:#f7f8fa}h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.2}section,article,details{background:white;border:1px solid #aab5c0;border-radius:8px;padding:14px;margin:14px 0}.cards{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px}.cards article{flex:1;min-width:190px}label{display:block;margin-top:12px;font-weight:600}textarea,select,button{font:inherit}textarea{display:block;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;min-height:76px}select{max-width:100%}button{padding:8px 12px;margin:8px 6px 8px 0;cursor:pointer}button:disabled{cursor:default}button:focus-visible,textarea:focus-visible,select:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #185ca0;outline-offset:3px}.notice{background:#edf3f8;padding:12px}.small{font-size:.9em}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:inherit;margin:6px 0}dialog{max-width:650px;width:calc(100% - 70px);border:2px solid #34495e;border-radius:8px}dialog::backdrop{background:#0008}[hidden]{display:none!important}</style></head><body><h1>Reasoning when evidence conflicts</h1><p class="notice">Rehearsal candidate requiring human review and interaction testing. No learning results or approvals exist. No grades, rankings or automatic judgments.</p><section><h2>1. Inspect fictional evidence</h2><p>Fictional period: 14 days. Water amounts are arbitrary story units per day, not plant-care advice.</p><div class="cards"><article><h3>A</h3><p class="small">Invented classroom story: these numbers are story inputs, not study results.</p><p>Water: 1<br>Light: bright<br>Final height: 12 cm<br>Leaves: upright</p></article><article><h3>B</h3><p class="small">Invented classroom story: these numbers are story inputs, not study results.</p><p>Water: 2<br>Light: dim<br>Final height: 18 cm<br>Leaves: drooping</p></article><article id="cardC" hidden><h3>C — additional evidence</h3><p class="small">Invented classroom story: these numbers are story inputs, not study results.</p><p>Water: 2<br>Light: bright<br>Final height: 10 cm<br>Leaves: upright</p></article></div><button id="reveal" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="cardC">Reveal C: compare with another observation</button><p id="missing">Starting heights, plant type, soil and other conditions are unrecorded. Final height is not an increase. Leaf descriptions do not establish health. “Better” needs a criterion. These cards do not isolate causes.</p><details><summary>Optional comparison hint</summary><p>A/B differ in recorded water and light. With C visible, compare A/C and B/C. Similar recorded conditions do not establish equal unrecorded conditions. C challenges “more water always accompanies greater final height”; it does not refute every claim.</p></details></section><section><h2>2. Explain or discuss</h2><p class="notice">People nearby can see this screen. Use fictional evidence; do not enter names or personal details. You may discuss, draw or use paper without entering text. Passing preserves access and a later contribution opportunity.</p><p>What differs in observations and recorded conditions? Which observation supports your wording? All entries are optional. Initial wording is editable working text, not an authenticated first thought.</p><div id="work"><label for="suggestion">Optional suggested wording — inspecting it changes no entry</label><select id="suggestion"><option value="">Use my own wording in the fields below</option><option>B is taller at the end.</option><option>Taller means better.</option><option>I cannot decide yet.</option></select><label for="target">Insert suggestion into</label><select id="target"><option value="initial">Initial wording</option><option value="current">Current claim</option></select><button id="insert">Insert selected wording</button><p class="small">Suggestions are prompts, not verified answers. Occupied fields require confirmation.</p><label for="initial">Initial wording</label><textarea id="initial" autocomplete="off"></textarea><label for="current">Current claim — retain or change it as you choose</label><textarea id="current" autocomplete="off"></textarea><label for="comparison">Pair compared and changed recorded conditions</label><textarea id="comparison" autocomplete="off"></textarea><label for="support">Supporting observation</label><textarea id="support" autocomplete="off"></textarea><label for="uncertainty">Uncertainty or information needed</label><textarea id="uncertainty" autocomplete="off"></textarea><label for="dissent">Optional alternative wording or dissent</label><textarea id="dissent" autocomplete="off"></textarea><label for="reconsider">Reconsideration description</label><select id="reconsider"><option>Not selected</option><option>Retain</option><option>Narrow</option><option>Revise</option><option>Withhold</option></select><label for="representation">Whose explanation does this represent? No names.</label><select id="representation"><option>Representation unresolved</option><option>One explanation</option><option>Several explanations</option></select><p>These descriptions do not verify agreement. Invite correction and preserve disagreement.</p><h3>Temporary recovery within this group</h3><p>Only the preceding replaced wording for each target is retained. Restoration requires confirmation and consumes its copy.</p><button id="restoreInitial" disabled>Restore previous initial wording</button><pre id="savedInitial"></pre><button id="restoreCurrent" disabled>Restore previous current claim</button><pre id="savedCurrent"></pre></div><p>Optional practice: Choose another pair. What can you claim, and what remains uncertain? Earlier prompts remain available. This is supported practice, not evidence of independence or transfer.</p><button id="preview">Preview current discussion wording</button></section><section><h2>3. Correctable discussion preview</h2><p>Working wording for discussion; it does not verify contribution, agreement or learning. Correct the fields above or leave disagreement unresolved. Completion is not evidence of scientific reasoning.</p><div id="output" hidden></div></section><section><h2>Paper-only alternative</h2><p>A teacher can copy A/B/C onto separate sheets; reveal C here to prepare its sheet, then hold that sheet until requested in the paper activity. Every sheet keeps the invented-story label and missing-information notice. Put suggested claims on separate slips.</p><p>Optional response sheet: Initial wording; Current claim; Pair and changed conditions; Supporting observation; Uncertainty; Alternative wording/dissent; Retain/narrow/revise/withhold; Whose explanation is represented?</p><p>Discuss orally, draw, point with explanation or use supported recording. Make recorder wording available for correction. Continue on paper after device failure without mandatory re-entry. Paper also has visibility limits; equivalence between routes is unknown.</p></section><section><h2>Shared-device handoff</h2><p>Refresh or closing loses temporary writing. Clear removes application-owned entries, previews, pending proposals and recovery copies. It cannot retract copies or what others saw. Browser-managed undo and autofill remain untested; this is not secure erasure.</p><button id="clear">Clear for next group…</button></section><p id="status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><dialog id="confirm" aria-labelledby="dialogTitle"><h2 id="dialogTitle"></h2><pre id="dialogText"></pre><button id="accept">Confirm</button><button id="cancel">Cancel</button></dialog><script>/* Candidate only. No storage, telemetry, network or evaluation. Human interaction checks remain pending. */
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id),work=$('work'),template=work.innerHTML,dlg=$('confirm');
const fields=['initial','current','comparison','support','uncertainty','dissent'];
