idence streams and specify a comparison method before any learning claim. This Measurement expert draft adds descriptive task lenses, comparison safeguards and coverage checks. No checks were executed; human review and all field evidence remain pending.","objections":["Hypothetical teacher dissent: paper-only discussion may leave more time for reasoning than instrument administration.","Rivals: apparent improvement may reflect cue familiarity, copying, recorder influence or teacher assistance.","Unknowns: language access, reading burden, device availability, discussion norms and task comparability."],"prototype_html":"","revisit_stage":"","risks":["Copied limitations or fluent recorder wording may resemble reasoning evidence.","Route selection, teacher assistance and prior familiarity can confound comparisons.","Absent subgroup evidence may be misreported as equitable access."],"system_capabilities":["Keep discussion previews separate from any external review worksheet; add no participant telemetry.","Expose evidence, optional hints and correction without scores or competence judgments.","Support synthetic transition checks and matching paper materials without personal records."],"tradeoffs":["Comparable prompts improve interpretation but can reproduce cueing.","Minimal collection protects dignity but limits subgroup conclusions.","Fresh transfer tasks reduce rehearsal effects but introduce unfamiliar vocabulary."]},"seq":42,"stage":"instrument"}]
