Transfer, coverage and unknowns
A fresh fictional task should change the evidence structure, rather than repeat the plant story's counterexample pattern. An open prompt with evidence and language supports available can examine reasoning in that task; immediate performance cannot establish retention. A separately reviewed delayed task is needed for any retention claim. Neither establishes broad transfer without further evidence.
Review coverage across paper/shared-device routes, reading and language presentation, oral/drawing/written contributions and discussion arrangements. Mark planned, observed and unknown coverage separately. No coverage is observed here. Do not infer disability or ability from route choice. If a relevant context is absent, withhold conclusions about it rather than treating missing complaints as equitable access.

Decision and human gates
