fore real participation."],"message":"Sequence 51 preserves human gates, but Evaluate also needs explicit rules for withholding conclusions when checks, comparison evidence or participation coverage are absent. Sequences 37 and 44 supply a candidate and protocol, not findings. I propose a claim-by-claim evidence ledger that separates untested behavior, task reasoning, access, workload and transfer. This is a Measurement expert draft for the rehearsal. No checks, participant observations, approvals or measured results exist; field evidence remains pending.","objections":["Hypothetical teacher dissent: “Paper cards support this discussion without administering another evaluation process.” Preserve paper-only delivery.","Rival explanations: fluent wording may reflect copying or recorder assistance; sparse wording may reflect reading, language, typing or discussion pressure.","Unknowns: task comparability, classroom languages, device access, discussion norms, coverage and acceptable workload."],"prototype_html":"","revisit_stage":"","risks":["An empty results record could be interpreted as evidence of no problems.","Copied limitations or group wording could be attributed to individual understanding.","Route selection, assistance and repeated exposure could produce misleading comparisons."],"system_capabilities":["Keep optional discussion wording separate from external evaluation records; collect no participant telemetry.","Expose invented evidence, supplied hints and correction without automatic reasoning judgments.","Preserve the paper route and synthetic interaction checks without learner identities, grades or rankings."],"tradeoffs":["Less explanatory cueing improves interpretation but can increase task demands.","Minimal collection protects dignity while limiting coverage claims.","Matching facilitation aids comparison but may obscure differences in ordinary workload."]},"seq":57,"stage":"evaluate"},{"agent":"orchestrator","response":{"advantages":["Claim-specific records distinguish documented design changes from tested behavior and learning.","Correction, optional recording and preserved dissent support learner choice.","A complete paper option permits review of whether browser controls justify their demands."],"artifact_body":"Status and evaluation conclusion
