Review preparation, facilitation, correction and recovery effort alongside opportunities to inspect, contribute and dissent. Preserve disagreement about whether instrumentation is worth its burden. Any real collection needs a separately reviewed purpose, minimum information, access, retention and correction process. Teacher, student and caregiver review and human interaction testing remain pending; no pilot or launch is authorized.","artifact_title":"Instrument expert draft: task evidence, comparison and coverage","challenged_assumption":"Successful interactions and polished discussion wording can support claims about reasoning, transfer or equitable access without a specified comparison and coverage method.","decision":"Continue Instrument by preparing the external synthetic worksheet and comparison/coverage drafts for review. Execute no checks or participant inquiry in this turn; retain all human gates and field evidence as pending.","drawbacks":["Manual review and separate transfer tasks require facilitator time.","Shared wording cannot establish each learner's reasoning.","Comparable tasks and participation routes remain unvalidated."],"evidence_refs":[20,22,35,37],"flourishing":["Agency and dignity: declining recording, retaining claims and dissent remain legitimate.","Access and belonging: investigate who can inspect, contribute and correct across routes.","Sustainable workload and learning/transfer: examine facilitation effort separately from reasoning and delayed performance."],"human_capabilities":["Reviewers must distinguish observed task behavior, interpretation and missing evidence.","Facilitators must preserve access supports, correction, dissent and optional participation.","Teacher, student and caregiver reviewers must examine any proposed inquiry before real use."],"message":"Sequence 37 proposes synthetic interaction review, but technical correctness cannot establish reasoning, equitable participation or transfer. Instrument should separate these evidence streams and specify a comparison method before any learning claim. This Measurement expert draft adds descriptive task lenses, comparison safeguards and coverage checks. No checks were executed; human review and all field evidence remain pending.","objections":["Hypothetical teacher dissent: paper-only discussion may leave more time for reasoning than instrument administration.","Rivals: apparent improvement may reflect cue familiarity, copying, recorder influence or teacher assistance.","Unknowns: language access, reading burden, device availability, discussion norms and task comparability."],"prototype_html":"","revisit_stage":"","risks":["Copied limitations or fluent recorder wording may resemble reasoning evidence.","Route selection, teacher assistance and prior familiarity can confound comparisons.","Absent subgroup evidence may be misreported as equitable access."],"system_capabilities":["Keep discussion previews separate from any external review worksheet; add no participant telemetry.","Expose evidence, optional hints and correction without scores or competence judgments.","Support synthetic transition checks and matching paper materials without personal records."],"tradeoffs":["Comparable prompts improve interpretation but can reproduce cueing.","Minimal collection protects dignity but limits subgroup conclusions.","Fresh transfer tasks reduce rehearsal effects but introduce unfamiliar vocabulary."]},"seq":42,"stage":"instrument"},{"agent":"orchestrator","response":{"advantages":["Separate evidence streams prevent technical checks from becoming learning claims.","Explicit expected behaviors make correction, cancellation and handoff reviewable.","Paper-only comparison preserves a complete non-AI option."],"artifact_body":"This is an integrated Instrument draft for a rehearsal, not an approved inquiry protocol. Sequence 37 supplies the unexecuted Build candidate; 35 specifies transition review; 42 adds separate evidence streams, comparison safeguards and coverage. Sequences 20 and 22 bound learning claims and collection. No real observations, measured results, approvals or demonstrated proficiency exist. Field evidence remains pending.

