objections":["Hypothetical teacher dissent: separating translation from explanation during discussion may be impractical.","Rival explanation: a learner may already understand the inference but use the facilitator's wording.","Unknowns: classroom languages, support practices and reviewer agreement remain unexamined."],"prototype_html":"","revisit_stage":"instrument","risks":["A supplied inference could be credited as learner reasoning.","Reviewers could withdraw needed support to obtain cleaner evidence.","Detailed assistance records could become unauthorized learner histories."],"system_capabilities":["Keep external review categories separate from optional browser wording.","Add no learner tracking, support scores or automatic assistance classification.","Retain fictional evidence, correction and the complete paper route."],"tradeoffs":["Accessible explanation versus attribution of reasoning to the learner.","Useful support descriptions versus minimal collection.","Consistent review categories versus context-sensitive interpretation."]}},"prev_hash":"4116f3e324bb8a82c3d750a44a4329e5f75b041f0881dd98c13ae280efb0a3d4","seq":62,"stage":"evaluate"}
