ance relative to a specific reasoning claim, include mixed and unknown support, and withhold unsupported attribution. It preserves 44's separate evidence streams and synthetic checks. The revision request is addressed at the specification level; application, human review and field evidence remain pending.","objections":["Hypothetical teacher dissent: assistance documentation may consume discussion time; paper-only facilitation without individual collection remains legitimate.","Rivals: wording may reflect existing understanding, imitation, newly adopted explanation or recorder influence.","Unknowns: languages, reading burden, device access, discussion norms, reviewer interpretation and acceptable workload."],"prototype_html":"","revisit_stage":"","risks":["Supplied notices or inferences could be credited as independent reasoning.","Reviewers could withdraw access support to simplify interpretation.","External worksheets could become unauthorized learner histories."],"system_capabilities":["Keep review records outside the candidate; add no tracking or automatic support classification.","Retain fictional evidence, optional wording and literal previews without consequential judgments.","Support synthetic correction and handoff checks; execution remains untested."],"tradeoffs":["Support improves participation while complicating attribution.","Brief records reduce workload but may omit assistance content.","Minimal collection protects dignity while limiting coverage conclusions."]},"seq":67,"stage":"instrument"},{"agent":"systems","response":{"advantages":["Separating facilitation from inquiry protects discussion time and support.","Prepared paper materials provide recovery without browser re-entry.","A revision manifest makes mismatched instructions reviewable."],"artifact_body":"This is a Systems engineer expert draft for the rehearsal, not an approved requirement. Build 37 remains unexecuted. Deploy 51 leaves decision ownership and classroom conditions pending. Instrument 67 resolves mixed-assistance attribution at the specification level; it supplies no evidence that its documentation is workable during discussion. No participant observations, human approvals, measured results or demonstrated proficiency exist. Field evidence remains pending.

The coupling challenge is divided attention. A facilitator may need to expose recorder wording, support language access, invite dissent, supervise replacement and clearing, and describe assistance relative to each reasoning claim. More instructions or facilitator training alone cannot establish capacity for these simultaneous duties. Refine should change the operating arrangement and documentation demands before interpreting apparent compliance as readiness.

Proposed requirement change: separate facilitation from inquiry. Before, the combined packet carries discussion duties and detailed external claim records without an explicit operating-mode boundary. After, facilitation mode uses the fictional evidence and optional discussion prompts without individual reasoning records. Inquiry mode is a separately reviewed proposal with an identified recording role, purpose and collection boundaries. These are activity arrangements, never learner classifications. If inquiry documentation competes with evidence access, support, correction or dissent, pause inquiry recording and continue discussion. Missing records then limit conclusions; they do not justify withdrawing support or pressuring entry. No staffing assignment is made here.

Human requirements: a facilitator must have prepared paper materials and the ability to stop browser activity without requiring learners to justify their route choice. Recorder wording must remain available for correction through the chosen mode; unresolved disagreement need not be entered on the shared screen. Any proposed inquiry needs a reviewed arrangement for observation and documentation that does not presume spare facilitator attention. Reviewers must examine preparation, discussion, correction and recovery effort separately. Acceptable effort and staffing remain unresolved; do not invent time thresholds.

System and package requirements: identify the candidate revision together with its paper cards, prompt sheet, support inventory and external review instructions. Distinguish an instrumentation-only revision from a browser behavior change. A change to supplied hints, replacement, clearing or paper prompts requires review of affected instructions and attribution examples. Retain existing exclusions: no identities, telemetry, grades, rankings, inferred disability or automatic support classification. A manifest establishes traceability, not compatibility or approval.

Recovery contract: prepare labelled A/B/C sheets before the activity, with C separately available for requested reveal. Keep invented-story labels and missing-condition notices. On device failure, continue orally or on paper without mandatory reconstruction or re-entry. Offer learners the choice to restate, change or leave lost wording unrecovered. Refresh loss cannot be repaired by the candidate's replacement recovery. Confirmed handoff clearing removes application-owned copies only; browser-managed retention and prior visibility remain unresolved. Any participant collection or actual-use decision remains subject to 51's separate human gates.

The complete non-AI option is teacher-facilitated paper discussion using these cards, separate suggestion slips and optional claim, comparison, uncertainty and dissent spaces. It may be selected from the outset. Paper has visibility and workload limits too; route equivalence is unknown.

Reviewable next action: prepare an external fictional walkthrough covering ordinary discussion, an assistance episode that supplies a target inference, occupied-field correction and device loss before handoff. For each transition record intended human responsibility, system behavior, competing duty, continuation route and unresolved question. Expected and observed behavior must stay separate; all outcomes are currently untested. Compare the proposed facilitation arrangement with paper-only delivery without claiming either is superior.

